  "body": "**No \u03ba claim and no word.** Knowledge package `research/helper-minimality/`: frame-side lower bounds for the helper layers of the frontier words, each with its scope and hypotheses, plus a single `verify.sh` that rechecks them. It continues #717 (rows F3-F5 there are the value-side records) and the merged #595.\n\n## What is shown (22 rows: 13 CHECKED, 4 ARGUED, 5 RECORDED)\n\n| Layer | Result | Scope |\n|---|---|---|\n| S1 scratch | In each of the 11 eight-line blocks of #656, 15 registers are infeasible: whole-bound registers \u2265 plane stoppers = 8, perfect matching forced, every whole-bound register (the \"never read\" ones too) is indispensable; the 38 \"twin\" couriers are whole-bound registers of this kind (38/38), none equal to its partner (value-forced, B176). CP-SAT (F\u2083 relaxation, dyadic coefficients, 4-level lemma argued in the card; any horizon) confirms for block (4,5,6,7): dropping 433 is INFEASIBLE. | given the shipped end-of-A frames as bounds (own 24 registers), FOM; true-cap case open |\n| S3/S4 copies | No copy pair can be merged by any reordering: 268/268 FAIL on #656 and on #799 (Lawler 1973 backward rule, checked against exhaustive search); every copy already has a two-visit conflict. | FOM; shipped-order partner frames `g` (lower bound for arbitrary reorderings only where value-forced, B172 caveat); rerun skipping the 1921 / 2317 value-zero adds is still 268/268 FAIL on #656 / #799 |\n| Bridges, holders | The 12 bridge registers 716..727: 12/12 FAIL; holder/entering copies 450..457 and 484..569: 94/94 FAIL. | #799, FOM |\n| Cut | Under H-CUT (justified by the spec lines `03-motifs.tex:78-83` and the emitter line `hpe_emit_local.py:94`, which are checked at the quoted lines), the cut needs \u2265 \u03bc \u2265 \u03c9 = 8 centres; both shipped words attain 8 = rank(F\u2212F\u2080). | #656, #799 |\n| Pre-read | Minimum touched pre-read targets on #799 within the 271-move family is 66 (CP-SAT OPTIMAL, bound 66) against threshold 62. | pairs / recorded triples only |\n| Model | The oracle frames equal the AL frames on all 5726 A/B ops of the #656 word (B128). | #656 chain word |\n\nThe S1 bound (given the shipped end-of-A frames) and the Lawler bounds (under the `g` hypothesis in the table) are support/frame bounds, so they hold for cancelling programs of the same op multiset too (contrast Boyar\u2013Find 2013); undo/redo ADDs change the multiset and are open.\n\n## Open gaps, stated plainly\n\n1. S1 blocks (0,1,2,3), (0,1,4,5), (0,1,6,7): the Hall bound is slack (21/21 matching with line registers alone); minimality of their 48 scratch registers is unproven, not refuted. B177 is running; no verdict yet.\n2. Multiset-changing merges (undo/redo ADDs, holder merges) are outside every Lawler result.\n3. S1 minimality is given the shipped end-of-A frames as bounds: the true-cap case (later readers' true caps replace them, as in #717) is open, as is an interface change; H-CUT is not enforced by AL (a centre-free toy is accepted by AL and flagged by the H-CUT check).\n4. Decoder n \u2265 9 (#717 D1) is a separate question and not covered.\n5. Pre-read is checked to singles, all pairs and recorded triple probes, not arbitrary k-sets.\n6. The Lawler layers and the S1 lemma have no independent second-reader audit.\n\n## Verification\n\n`bash research/helper-minimality/verify.sh /fresh/dir` from a fresh `git archive`: 53 PASS lines (2 in step 0), 0 FAIL, exit 0, about 52 s. Step 0 checks every file against `MANIFEST.sha256` and every vendored input against `SOURCES.json` (git blob ids of the #799 / #635 / main files, hashes published by #656 / #799 for the rebuilt words) and stops on any mismatch (tamper test: a changed byte in a word or in a script exits 1 at step 0). `HM_FULL=1` also regenerates the 36,501-pair pre-read table. No absolute paths, no personal names, no \u03ba claim.\n\n## Credit\n\nBuilds on #717 and #595 (DreamingOfClouds); the words and verifier are #656, #659, #664, #799, #741, #685 (jeremykothe2, chafreaky), #645 (icekylinx), #622/#623/#635 (jeremykothe2); related: #698 (thakrarsagar; fixed gate order, exact end-of-B frames, against the order-free bounds here), #719 (rank-two obstruction for the 78 CK cleanup pairs), #705 (littleBro; different model and argument), #687 (cbethin), #683 (Mister-Meeseeks), #869/#870 (jeremykothe2). See `NOTICE.md`.\n\nPrepared by DreamingOfClouds with Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), via Claude Code; Apache-2.0.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
